    with: "If the **Catalogue service** (or its backing database) in this repository were updated (e.g., changing container image tags, ports, database credentials, or API contracts), the following services, backing stores, deployment manifests, Helm templates, service definitions, monitoring configs, and verification steps would be affected.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Services & Backing Stores\n* **Catalogue Microservice (`catalogue`)**: The core catalog HTTP API container (default image: `weaveworksdemos/catalogue:0.3.5`, port `80`).\n* **Catalogue Database (`catalogue-db`)**: The MySQL database backing store for catalog data (default image: `weaveworksdemos/catalogue-db:0.3.0`, database name: `socksdb`, port `3306`).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Kubernetes Manifests & Helm Templates\n\n#### Standalone Kubernetes Manifests\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/manifests/05-catalogue-dep.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/manifests/05-catalogue-dep.yaml): Catalogue Deployment manifest configuring container image `weaveworksdemos/catalogue:0.3.5`, command `/app -port=80`, security context, resources, and HTTP liveness/readiness probes on `/health`.\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/manifests/06-catalogue-svc.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/manifests/06-catalogue-svc.yaml): Catalogue Kubernetes Service definition exposing port `80` with Prometheus scrape annotations.\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/manifests/07-catalogue-db-dep.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/manifests/07-catalogue-db-dep.yaml): Catalogue Database Deployment manifest configuring `weaveworksdemos/catalogue-db:0.3.0` with `MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD` and `MYSQL_DATABASE=socksdb`.\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/manifests/08-catalogue-db-svc.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/manifests/08-catalogue-db-svc.yaml): Catalogue Database Kubernetes Service definition exposing MySQL port `3306`.\n\n#### Combined Kubernetes Manifest\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/complete-demo.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/complete-demo.yaml): Monolithic all-in-one Kubernetes manifest defining `catalogue` Deployment, `catalogue` Service, `catalogue-db` Deployment, and `catalogue-db` Service specs.\n\n#### Helm Chart Configurations & Templates\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/helm-chart/values.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/helm-chart/values.yaml): Helm values defining image repository (`weaveworksdemos/catalogue`), tag (`0.3.5`), `containerPort` (`80`), and resource limits for `catalogue`, as well as `cataloguedb` (`weaveworksdemos/catalogue-db:0.3.0`).\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/helm-chart/templates/catalogue-dep.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/helm-chart/templates/catalogue-dep.yaml): Helm template for generating the Catalogue Deployment.\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/helm-chart/templates/catalogue-svc.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/helm-chart/templates/catalogue-svc.yaml): Helm template for generating the Catalogue Service.\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/helm-chart/templates/catalogue-db-dep.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/helm-chart/templates/catalogue-db-dep.yaml): Helm template for generating the Catalogue Database Deployment.\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/helm-chart/templates/catalogue-db-svc.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/helm-chart/templates/catalogue-db-svc.yaml): Helm template for generating the Catalogue Database Service.\n\n#### Distributed Tracing & Jaeger Manifests\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/manifests-jaeger/catalogue-dep.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/manifests-jaeger/catalogue-dep.yaml): Specialized Catalogue Deployment manifest with Jaeger/Zipkin tracing endpoint configuration (`http://zipkin.jaeger.svc.cluster.local:9411/api/v1/spans`).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Docker Compose Services\n* [`deploy/docker-compose/docker-compose.yml`](microservices-demo/deploy/docker-compose/docker-compose.yml): Local multi-container Docker specification defining `catalogue` and `catalogue-db` service containers, environment variables, capabilities, and security flags.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Monitoring & Telemetry Dashboards\n* [`deploy/kubernetes/manifests-monitoring/20-grafana-configmap.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/manifests-monitoring/20-grafana-configmap.yaml): Grafana ConfigMap containing Prometheus query metrics for request latency quantiles and counts targeting `name=\"catalogue\"`.\n* [`deploy/docker-compose/grafana/sock-shop-performance-dashboard.json`](microservices-demo/deploy/docker-compose/grafana/sock-shop-performance-dashboard.json): Performance dashboard configuration tracking HTTP request rates and 2xx responses for `job=\"catalogue\"`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Verification & Health Check Steps\n\nWhen changing `catalogue` or `catalogue-db`, the following automated verification steps and test suites run against the service:\n\n1. **Kubernetes Liveness & Readiness Probes**:\n   * Evaluates HTTP GET request responses on `/health` at port `80` (configured in [`deploy/kubernetes/manifests/05-catalogue-dep.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/manifests/05-catalogue-dep.yaml) and [`deploy/kubernetes/complete-demo.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/complete-demo.yaml)).\n\n2. **Automated Healthcheck Test Suite**:\n   * [`healthcheck/healthcheck.rb`](microservices-demo/healthcheck/healthcheck.rb): Ruby integration script that verifies service health by making HTTP requests to `/<service>/health` and asserting that returned status is `\"OK\"`.\n   * [`healthcheck/Dockerfile`](microservices-demo/healthcheck/Dockerfile): Docker image recipe that packages and executes `healthcheck.rb` during CI/CD verification runs.\n\n3. **End-to-End Load Verification**:\n   * [`deploy/kubernetes/manifests-loadtest/loadtest-dep.yaml`](microservices-demo/deploy/kubernetes/manifests-loadtest/loadtest-dep.yaml): Locust load-testing deployment running continuous user interaction flows against the application front-end (`http://front-end.sock-shop.svc.cluster.local`), exercising downstream calls to the catalogue microservice.",
